{"name":"Gossamer","hex":"#399f86","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gossamer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fine film made up of cobwebs, seen floating in the air or caught on bushes, etc.","A soft, sheer fabric."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tenuous, light, filmy or delicate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gossamer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spider silk","blocks":[{"text":"Spider silk is a protein fibre or silk spun by spiders. Spiders use silk to make webs or other structures that function as adhesive traps to catch prey, to entangle and restrain prey before biting, to transmit tactile information, or as nests or cocoons to protect their offspring. They can use the silk to suspend themselves from height, to float through the air, or to glide away from predators. Most spiders vary the thickness and adhesiveness of their silk according to its use."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Argiope_bruennichi_Cornacchiaia_1.jpg/330px-Argiope_bruennichi_Cornacchiaia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider_silk","wikidata":"Q2740926"},{"title":"Glossary of textile manufacturing","blocks":[{"text":"The manufacture of textiles is one of the oldest of human technologies. To make textiles, the first requirement is a source of fiber from which a yarn can be made, primarily by spinning. The yarn is processed by knitting or weaving, with color and patterns, which turns it into cloth. The machine used for weaving is the loom. For decoration, the process of coloring yarn or the finished material is dyeing. For more information of the various steps, see textile manufacturing."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_textile_manufacturing","wikidata":"Q1153166"},{"title":"Gossamer (Looney Tunes)","blocks":[{"text":"Gossamer is a fictional cartoon character in the Warner Bros. Looney Tunes and Merrie Melodies series of cartoons. He is a large, hairy, orange or red monster. His body is perched on two giant tennis shoes, and his heart-shaped face is composed of only two oval eyes and a wide mouth, with two hulking arms ending in dirty, clawed fingers. The monster's main trait is his uncombed, orange hair. He originally was voiced by Mel Blanc and has been voiced by Frank Welker, Maurice LaMarche, Joe Alaskey, Jim Cummings, Kwesi Boakye, Eric Bauza and currently Fred Tatasciore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/77/Gossamer_restored.jpg/330px-Gossamer_restored.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gossamer_(Looney_Tunes)","wikidata":"Q2357888"},{"title":"Gossamer (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Gossamer (2006) is a novel with elements of both fantasy and realism for young adults by Lois Lowry."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fc/Gossamer_%28novel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gossamer_(novel)","wikidata":"Q5587471"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/J%C3%B3zef_Che%C5%82mo%C5%84ski_-_Indian_summer_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-J%C3%B3zef_Che%C5%82mo%C5%84ski_-_Indian_summer_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/J%C3%B3zef_Che%C5%82mo%C5%84ski_-_Indian_summer_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-J%C3%B3zef_Che%C5%82mo%C5%84ski_-_Indian_summer_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/J%C3%B3zef_Che%C5%82mo%C5%84ski_-_Indian_summer_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-J%C3%B3zef_Che%C5%82mo%C5%84ski_-_Indian_summer_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c